1
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:29,333
Misery loves family.

2
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:52,666
Meet the Fockers is a comedy, romance film directed by Jay Roach.

3
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Hard-to-crack ex-CIA man Jack Byrnes and his wife Dina head for the warmer climes of
Florida to meet the parents of their son-in-law-to-be, Greg Focker.

4
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
Unlike their happily matched offspring, the future in-laws find themselves
in a situation of opposites that definitely do not attract.

5
00:31:56,666 --> 00:32:02,666
Greg Focker, played by Ben Stiller.

6
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Jack Byrnes, played by Robert De Niro.

7
00:44:43,333 --> 00:44:49,333
Bernie Focker, played by Dustin Hoffman.

8
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Rozalin Focker, played by Barbra Streisand.

9
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Dina Byrnes, played by Blythe Danner.

10
01:03:53,333 --> 01:03:59,333
Pam Byrnes, played by Teri Polo.

11
01:10:16,666 --> 01:10:22,666
Meet the Fockers is a 2004 American romantic comedy film directed by Jay Roach.

12
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The second in the Fockers film series, it features Robert De Niro, Ben Stiller, Blythe Danner and Teri Polo reprising their
roles from the first film, with Dustin Hoffman and Barbra Streisand joining the cast as Greg Focker's parents.

13
01:23:03,333 --> 01:23:09,333
Meet the Fockers was released on December 22, 2004, in
the United States by Universal Pictures.

14
01:29:26,666 --> 01:29:32,666
It received mixed reviews, and was a box-office success, grossing $522
million and becoming the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2004.

15
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
A further sequel, Little Fockers, followed in 2010.

16
01:42:13,333 --> 01:42:19,333
The film explores themes of florida, central intelligence agency (cia),
nurse, parent child relationship, anti-authoritarian upbringing.

17
01:48:36,666 --> 01:48:42,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
